nt :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$t=4$ and $t=5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401718} :answer-field/id #uuid "5695dc0f-925d-5609-ad66-b2dab30bc5b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401716}] :question/id #uuid "0c6851eb-a487-5113-99b9-8f1c04863168" :question/math-academy-id "q-18246" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}t & -8 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}t & -8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =t\\cdot 9-(-8)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =9t-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9t-8 & ={t}^{2}+12 \\\\ {t}^{2}-9t+20 & =0 \\\\ (t-5)(t-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=4$ and $t=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1003d7e-42ef-59a2-9038-178e1c676be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2y &=10 \\\\ - x + y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058993} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ded7fa-c1f6-5aad-8a94-f332f052ff6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2y &=0 \\\\ - x + y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058994} {:answer/id #uuid "e51ccf34-2862-5dcc-bb64-f8f734bc2e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2y &=10 \\\\ x + y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058995} {:answer/id #uuid "eac00324-c2df-502b-b5dd-ba0a44acfb6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2y &=1 \\\\ - x + y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058996} {:answer/id #uuid "038c96de-d924-5dda-835b-036092e680cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2y &=10 \\\\ x + y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058997}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f473abb5-e351-5444-b66f-186a774f8f2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64df3633-b59c-5a2c-a47b-ac990893af30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=0 \\\\ -x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403490} {:answer/id #uuid "bd635cf4-1b1c-55e3-b846-cf1074404d1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=10 \\\\ x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403491} {:answer/id #uuid "f08977b3-da5b-5a3f-9b5f-51a1b0b73af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=10 \\\\ -x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403492} {:answer/id #uuid "d79b540e-61c1-524a-aada-7bc8f0c88fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=10 \\\\ x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403493} {:answer/id #uuid "a1094fb0-5cb4-5005-a45b-91f8fd20411a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=1 \\\\ -x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=10 \\\\ -x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403492} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc9e5b69-52ca-5647-a69d-a0b8ed7e52f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403489}] :question/id #uuid "611f1d4a-3c30-50c6-9215-73810a99de02" :question/math-academy-id "q-71724" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and  $y$,  the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=10 \\\\ -x+y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8868f167-119b-5e73-bc65-40becaf6c2b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059335} {:answer/id #uuid "e74bb0c6-bc63-5059-84dc-eb9b59596b2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059336} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f4f4af-05d0-53f1-8ebb-4276ab2ed9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059337} {:answer/id #uuid "21f238e5-ba0c-57b7-8096-4d2e15910cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059338} {:answer/id #uuid "51967300-99d9-5ef0-a07f-ecc5ed2d01a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059339}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a645da-29fd-5221-a5e3-74f151b09fe2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059334}] :question/id #uuid "7121e717-26c8-5ebd-a468-32df5efb3e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-979" :question/problem "What is $5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6c7feb-e1e4-5887-9269-a70c549b3932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361110} {:answer/id #uuid "4da79416-6947-54f4-88ab-d36dbb592119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361174} {:answer/id #uuid "53376dd3-6051-57be-9178-00766c6ec74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361206} {:answer/id #uuid "69e380fe-b63f-5b7d-8e40-f4c2783aa85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361312} {:answer/id #uuid "83d9f12d-1a74-5c6d-b0b8-9182fdd9e2a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361174} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5735c9d-1438-5c01-a0eb-1e4ffee8d379" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362137}] :question/id #uuid "00d4f637-689d-5f49-8309-b4f927af6909" :question/math-academy-id "q-981" :question/problem "If $kA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -21 & 56\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhere $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-k & -3k & 8k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-k & -3k & 8k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -21 & 56\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the leftmost elements, $-k$ and $-7.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =-7 \\\\ k & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7553ef1-51c2-54a9-8614-83ddaa42949e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 12 \\\\ -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059365} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d8d5fa-05d0-53ef-8422-383bbcceea56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059366} {:answer/id #uuid "512801ed-6f3a-591f-b7cb-c4cbe83c0761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059367} {:answer/id #uuid "572809ce-d046-5a24-9f10-148f0a5e4ab9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059368} {:answer/id #uuid "69f57a2d-9ef8-5200-94ba-c0a806446d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059369}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ee9f14cd-76b1-523a-ad55-ec7f6fa284cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059364}] :question/id #uuid "5e067766-b48f-598d-88cc-5fd88e9b7386" :question/math-academy-id "q-986" :question/problem "Calculate $6D$, if\n$D = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 4\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060926 :tutorial/content "We can multiply matrices by numbers. This type of multiplication is known as **scalar multiplication**. Here, a **scalar** is just a number.\n\nFor example, consider the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo multiply ${A}$ by the scalar $2,$ we just multiply each entry of ${A}$ by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 3 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, to multiply a $m \\times n$ matrix $A$ by a scalar $c,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $c$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & … & {a}_{1n} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & … & {a}_{2n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ {a}_{m1} & {a}_{m2} & … & {a}_{mn}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d7efb59b-c6d7-5c06-97f3-b19ec863c9eb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2975 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186061006 :tutorial/content "How do we find the determinant of a $3\\times3$ matrix such as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nOne way to do this is to take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & ={{(\\,7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{11}}\\cdot \\overset{{M}_{11}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}}}-{{(\\,1\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{12}}\\cdot \\overset{{M}_{12}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{vmatrix}}}+{{(-3)}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{13}}\\cdot \\overset{{M}_{13}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}}} \\\\  & =7(-2-0)-1(-3-20)-3(0-10) \\\\  & =-14+23+30 \\\\  & =39\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the above, we have denoted $\\color{blue}M_{1j}$ as the minor of the entry ${\\color{red}a_{1j}}.$\n\nIn general, the determinant of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = {\\color{red}a_{11}}{\\color{blue}M_{11}} - {\\color{red}a_{12}}{\\color{blue}M_{12}} + {\\color{red}a_{13}}{\\color{blue}M_{13}}.\n$$\n\nThat is, if $\\begin{bmatrix}a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & i\\end{bmatrix}$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & i\\end{vmatrix} & =a\\begin{vmatrix}e & f \\\\ h & i\\end{vmatrix}-b\\begin{vmatrix}d & f \\\\ g & i\\end{vmatrix}+c\\begin{vmatrix}d & e \\\\ g & h\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =a(ei-fh)-b(di-fg)+c(dh-eg).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Important:** Do not forget about the *minus sign* in front of the *second term* in the formula!" :tutorial/id #uuid "99828b7b-b501-5509-8853-d17316824f5f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9175 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186061008 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the $3\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ k & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nthat has an unknown constant $k$ as one of the entries, and we are given that $A$ is singular. How do we find all the possible values of $k?$\n\nOne way is to use the formula for the determinant of a $3 \\times 3$ matrix to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k,$ and then make an equation with the given determinant to solve for $k.$\n\nSo first, let's use the formula for the determinant on our matrix to get an expression in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ k & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1-2)-2(k-0)+3(2k-0) \\\\  & =-3-2k+6k \\\\  & =4k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we are told that $\\det(A) =0,$ let's equate the above expression to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ k & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ 4k-3 & =0 \\\\ 4k & =3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only possible value for $k$ is $\\dfrac{3}{4}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "55643210-75d5-50e5-a63b-30b951b8a201" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9177 :tutorial/title "Solving for a Variable"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087500 :question/id #uuid "6587b5f1-8a44-556a-a95e-20c54dfebc04" :question/math-academy-id "e-4367" :question/problem "What are the dimensions of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix ${A}$ has $4$ rows and $3$ columns. Therefore, its dimensions are $4\\times 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087501 :question/id #uuid "74a9046e-e0a3-59d6-8b13-437e9a0cf04a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4370" :question/problem "What are the dimensions of the matrix ${D},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix ${D}$ has $1$ row and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087502 :question/id #uuid "9c82456c-49ea-5a5e-b0a2-0ab17059acee" :question/math-academy-id "e-4390" :question/problem "Which of the following are zero matrices?\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a zero matrix since some of its entries are not zeros (for instance, $q_{12}=0.1\\neq0$).\n\n- $R$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are zero matrices."}]}
